  "result": "The six-question quiz on O4 is ready as `quizzes/0002.json`, and its key is `keys/0002.json`.\n\nIt is built on the makerspace assistant and has five multiple-choice items, one numeric item and one short-answer item.\n- **q1–q2:** tell a workflow from an agent by who owns the control flow, including a system that calls a model but is still a workflow.\n- **q3:** choose a fixed workflow for the booking steps, given your small model budget.\n- **q4:** work out the daily cost difference between a workflow and an agent loop.\n- **q5:** pick the request that really needs an agent.\n- **q6:** answer a teammate who wants everything built as an agent.\n\nThere is no lesson on O4 yet, so the quiz runs ahead of the lessons. I wrote it as a check of the objective itself. I did not read or cite an outside source for it, so the key rests on my own understanding of the workflow/agent distinction.\n\nThe key introduces misconception ids M7–M10 for errors specific to this objective, such as \"an agent is always better\" and \"using a model makes it an agent\". I did not check M2 and M5 against anything, since no file I read defines them. M1, M3, M4 and M6 appear in key 0001.\n\nWould you like a short lesson on O4 before you take the quiz, or do you want to take the quiz first?",
